# This repo's code runs on Linux (Proxmox nodes, WSL). Force LF in the working tree
# regardless of platform/autocrlf, so shell scripts and Ansible templates never get CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.j2        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.tf        text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.sources   text eol=lf
justfile    text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.editorconfig text eol=lf

# Binaries (none yet, but be explicit)
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary

# GENERATED, served as a binary marker in diffs (`-diff`), NOT excluded from review by policy:
# the dashboard ConfigMap keeps its whole JSON model on ONE line, so any regeneration rewrites
# a ~170 KB line and a two-target change becomes a ~340 KB hunk. On 2026-09-19 that alone put
# ailab#792 past both reviewer personas' size cap (507 KB, 27 of 27 files skipped). With -diff
# Gitea's .diff carries "Binary files differ" for it and reviewbot classifies that as binary,
# which it neither reviews nor holds against the verdict. Review the GENERATOR
# (scripts/gen-reporting-dashboard.py); `git diff` on the yaml itself stays available with
# `git diff --text`, and the dashboard-preview check renders the real thing.
kubernetes/apps/infrastructure/monitoring/reporting-dashboard.yaml -diff
